{"name":"Fairy Wand","hex":"#aea4c1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fairy wand","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flowering plant of species Chamaelirium luteum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairy_wand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chamaelirium","blocks":[{"text":"Chamaelirium is a genus of flowering plants in the family Melanthiaceae, native to eastern Asia and central and western northern America. Its synonyms include Chionographis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chamaelirium_luteum.jpg/330px-Chamaelirium_luteum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamaelirium"},{"title":"Fairy","blocks":[{"text":"A fairy is a type of mythical being or legendary creature, generally described as anthropomorphic, found in the folklore of multiple European cultures, a form of spirit, often with magical, metaphysical, supernatural, or preternatural qualities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg/330px-Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy"},{"title":"Wand","blocks":[{"text":"A wand is a thin, light-weight rod that is held with one hand, and is traditionally made of wood, but may also be made of other materials, such as metal, bone or stone. Long versions of wands are often styled in forms of staves or sceptres, which could have large ornamentation on the top."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG/330px-John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wand"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/James_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_for